\f1\fs22 Eloise allowed Hayley to go to the city under stringent conditions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 One: she would travel there, back, and travel about only by Shakti Enterprises hover-copts and chauffeured ground cars.\
Two: She would be attended at all times by a detail, any of whom would be terminated if they failed to keep Hayley always under surveillance and safe.\
Three: She would not attempt to contact any of her colleagues at TRAMPS.\
Hayley appreciated the first condition, laughed at the third, and asked Sarah for intel on the second.\
\'93Oh, those dentist assassins in her entourage? They\'92re definitely expendable,\'94 Sarah confirmed. \'93Please try not to get any of them killed.\'94\
Hayley solemnly promised and, as the fan noise of the hover-copt on the Sublime Point pad drowned out their voices, she kissed Sarah goodbye, then stood awkwardly in front of Kathy until Sarah almost pushed her off her feet and Kathy had to catch her. They had a moment, until Hayley regained her composure, straightened, and did that safety dance-step-crouch everyone performs as they approach a full-throated hover-copt.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93Excuse me.\'94 Hayley approached the great lumbering bear of a man, who turned and seemed to be working something out behind his eyes. After a second or so, he\'92d correctly assessed Hayley to be police, and said, \'93What can I do for you?\'94 with a weary tone.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93Stasis Anomalies Investigator Stockwell?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93What of it?\'94\
Hayley nodded; the man had confirmed his identity. \'93May I call you Chip?\'94\
Chip huffed. \'93You\'92d better be getting to the point, Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning.\'94\
Okay, so he already knew who she was, but Hayley wasn\'92t unsettled. \'93I believe you made a call on a family on Monday, 12
